Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:07:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Playerbots: actually vote on group loot rolls

The path was never finished - RollOnItemInSlot returned false unconditionally, LootStartRollAction filled the pending list through Loot::GetRollForSlot, a stub returning nullptr, and ActiveRolls::CleanUp used the same stub and therefore erased every entry the moment it was added. No bot ever voted and the countdown ran out on every single item.

This core keeps rolls in Group::RollId, so votes go through Group::CountRollVote - the same entry point the client uses. Group::GetActiveRoll gives the bots a read-only view without opening up the roll list.

Bots defer to the people in the group: they wait while any real player still has the dialog open, and they never roll need against a player who asked for need. If nobody clicks, they vote once half the countdown is gone so one absent player cannot make everyone sit out the timer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
